    "datasource": "Kodak Pro 100 / PRN, Pro 100T / PRT, Pro 400 / PPF, Pro 400 MC / PMC and Pro 1000 / PMZ colour negative films, publication E-182, February 1997; SHA256 43f9be571f731356d868993dce6760c1f0254d04c50bf09b761027c5d0bd60cc. Reproduce with scripts/bw_expansion/prepare_colour_film.py; axis calibration derived from the page by scripts/bw_expansion/extract_graphs.py; source points, assumptions and conditions: data/profile-sources/kodak-pro-1000-pmz/recipe.json. Dye spectra: kodak_portra_800 shapes, scaled so their mixture reproduces this sheet's own midscale-neutral-minus-D-min. PCHIP of the three plotted log-sensitivity traces; engine covers 380-780 nm, each trace is used only over its own plotted span and is unmeasured elsewhere. Relative shape only; the panel's E.N.D. density criterion is not an absolute speed. Measured, not assumed: the sheet's D-min trace is the spectral base density, and what the Status M densitometer reads through it is subtracted from the characteristic curves. Spectral adaptation parameters are not this stock's own: they are borrowed from kodak_portra_800. The same stock whose dye shapes this sheet is prepared with. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [1.0464, 1.0631, 0.9025], log-exposure shift [0.0142, 0.0, -0.2609], data_trustability 0.5. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 28.9% before, 5.4% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from the datasheet. The engine refused 1 trial correction(s) during the fit (note: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace); those points were treated as infeasible. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [1.0152, 1.0146, 0.9747], log-exposure shift [0.0016, 0.0, -0.0292], data_trustability 0.5. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 5.4% before, 4.4% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from the datasheet. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [1.0, 1.0, 1.0], log-exposure shift [0.0, 0.0, 0.0], data_trustability 0.5. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 4.4% before, 4.4% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from the datasheet."
